    {
      "post_id": 36893,
      "author_username": "beautytubes",
      "author_user_id": 961,
      "timestamp_iso": "2018-04-17T18:49:35+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1523990975000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 17, 2018 13:49:35 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "<p>And now the current status from Austria:</p><p><br/></p><p>My bog:</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/26gj1Sx\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/916/41523738771_8d65a5024b_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24UmGqV\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/789/40630258885_00c3077263_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>The first Droseras are out:</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/26cDphj\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/879/41482255302_cc7d81b573_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Pinguicula grandiflora:</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/26cDvgJ\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/874/41482275452_3d13b59082_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Drosophyllum lusitanicum:</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24UmZfr\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/870/40630315465_efed34e948_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>You from US should know this. It is growing in my filter and nutrition absorber for my bog (Lysichiton americanus):</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25bhsHW\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/940/40810496264_8bcdda96d8_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Another nice absorber ( Caltha palustris)</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25bhx3s\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/878/40810510794_dda43a3c20_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Somehow the number of purpureas grow in my collection continuousely!</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24UmMci\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/807/40630274915_c989d95161_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Puh it starts to become fresh outside, lets go into my greenhouse (somehow messy in the overview!):</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/23vrb4J\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/824/39714496120_8e58db9102_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>But the Details are great! I got the glue! The first flowers of D. californica after some years of trial and error:</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24UnchT\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/918/40630355975_775e22ded4_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>The dionaeas start to wake up</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/26cEgX7\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/809/41482425752_3744c673ae_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>The whole greenhouse stinks after the flavas now!</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/J8CpZb\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/873/27653304448_77fe0acbf8_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24UnEhV\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/939/40630446805_b9483b75f2_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24Unm5x\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/828/40630385535_f52606fafa_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/24Um8TF\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/835/40630149425_30e3433d89_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>THE GOLDIEEEE YEAHHHH (the tubes are close before opening and are really goldish yellow! Can't wait for them!)</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/GBjW9c\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/894/26654042227_3b1903e039_k.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Cant wait for the \"pop\"</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25bjN2w\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/875/40810951424_23f4173093_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>One from my dealer, bought last weekend.</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/25bh4q3\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/865/40810417854_ec968222a2_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/26cDbjW\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/843/41482211722_641b8d0a57_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>And two rubricorporas from my dealer (mine are not ready yet)</p><p><br/></p><p>Waccammaw like! (One day I will have one, it is soooo hard to get them here in Europe <img alt=\":(\" class=\"smile\" src=\"//storage.proboards.com/forum/images/smiley/sad.png\"/> ):</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/23vrhpE\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/897/39714517460_a3084d49f6_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Giant red throat!</p><p><br/></p><p><a href=\"https://flic.kr/p/GBkaNB\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/868/26654088187_b92b344106_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a></p><p><br/></p><p>Stay tuned!</p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p>",
      "body_text": "And now the current status from Austria:\nMy bog:\nThe first Droseras are out:\nPinguicula grandiflora:\nDrosophyllum lusitanicum:\nYou from US should know this. It is growing in my filter and nutrition absorber for my bog (Lysichiton americanus):\nAnother nice absorber ( Caltha palustris)\nSomehow the number of purpureas grow in my collection continuousely!\nPuh it starts to become fresh outside, lets go into my greenhouse (somehow messy in the overview!):\nBut the Details are great! I got the glue! The first flowers of D. californica after some years of trial and error:\nThe dionaeas start to wake up\nThe whole greenhouse stinks after the flavas now!\nTHE GOLDIEEEE YEAHHHH (the tubes are close before opening and are really goldish yellow! Can't wait for them!)\nCant wait for the \"pop\"\nOne from my dealer, bought last weekend.\nAnd two rubricorporas from my dealer (mine are not ready yet)\nWaccammaw like! (One day I will have one, it is soooo hard to get them here in Europe\n):\nGiant red throat!\nStay tuned!",
