    {
      "post_id": 36960,
      "author_username": "alexintx",
      "author_user_id": 993,
      "timestamp_iso": "2018-04-22T20:29:50+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1524428990000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Apr 22, 2018 15:29:50 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "<div author=\"@jwalker\" class=\"quote\" source=\"/post/36958/thread\" timestamp=\"1524413523\"><div class=\"quote_body\"><div class=\"quote_avatar_container\"><div class=\"avatar-wrapper avatar_size_quote avatar-418\" title=\"jwalker\"><img alt=\"jwalker Avatar\" src=\"//storage.proboards.com/forum/images/defaultavatar.png\"/></div></div><div class=\"quote_header\"><a href=\"/post/36958/thread\"><abbr class=\"o-timestamp time\" data-timestamp=\"1524413523000\" title=\"Apr 22, 2018 11:12:03 GMT -5\">Apr 22, 2018 11:12:03 GMT -5</abbr></a> <span itemscope=\"\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\"><a class=\"user-link js-user-link user-418 group-0\" href=\"/user/418\" itemprop=\"url\" title=\"@jwalker\"><span itemprop=\"name\">jwalker</span></a></span> said:</div>So I put my plants outside and came out this morning and the water was frozen. Great start to the season<div class=\"quote_clear\"></div></div></div>The only traps on my plants that haven't been bent badly in the middle by wind are my S. rosea and the shoots coming up from the bare rhizome. Sure, they're getting some nice color and stuff, but they look so sad with the tops leaning over... And I'm not at home to fix them. Basically, because of the delay in coming out of dormancy, some of the softer, flatter young pitchers got exposed to strong thunderstorm wind (causing the damage).<br/><br/>Hopefully this summer won't be hot enough to entirely shut down their growth. At least my VFTs look good.<br/>",
      "body_text": "Apr 22, 2018 11:12:03 GMT -5\njwalker\nsaid:\nSo I put my plants outside and came out this morning and the water was frozen. Great start to the season\nThe only traps on my plants that haven't been bent badly in the middle by wind are my S. rosea and the shoots coming up from the bare rhizome. Sure, they're getting some nice color and stuff, but they look so sad with the tops leaning over... And I'm not at home to fix them. Basically, because of the delay in coming out of dormancy, some of the softer, flatter young pitchers got exposed to strong thunderstorm wind (causing the damage).\nHopefully this summer won't be hot enough to entirely shut down their growth. At least my VFTs look good.",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://storage.proboards.com/forum/images/defaultavatar.png"
      ],
